{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'implementation' %}{% set plan_short = 'Implementation' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'From plan to work' %}
{% set plan_title = 'The first 100 days and Year One delivery plan' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Sequence the work, assign authority, verify costs and publish progress without waiting for every long-term question to be solved.' %}
{% set plan_status = 'Implementation framework' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Operating rule</p><h2>Every action needs an owner, deadline, cost, funding source, evidence and correction trigger.</h2><p class="plan-lede">Policy work can begin through existing capacity. Construction, technology, staffing and new programs move only after scope, operating cost, authority and funding are confirmed.</p></header></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Days 1 to 30</p><h2>Open the record and establish control.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Name accountable offices</h3><p>Assign one executive owner and one operational lead to every plan commitment.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Release governance baselines</h3><p>Publish the organization chart, committee mandates, records route and decision calendar.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Inventory active commitments</h3><p>List capital projects, company lending, debt, agreements, housing work and audit actions.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Freeze unsupported promises</h3><p>Do not announce cost or completion dates until scope, authority and funding are documented.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Days 31 to 60</p><h2>Reconcile money, capacity and delivery status.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Community wealth reconciliation</h3><p>Bring trust, debt, guarantees, company loans and member benefit into one statement.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Housing and infrastructure validation</h3><p>Confirm lots, water capacity, designs, budgets, contracts, funding and completion stages.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Department capacity check</h3><p>Confirm staff time, vacancies, dependencies and the work that must be externally scoped.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Enterprise reporting launch</h3><p>Issue the common quarterly template and reconcile opening balances by company.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Days 61 to 100</p><h2>Adopt the funded twelve-month work plan.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Approve costed packages</h3><p>Separate internal-capacity work, quoted work and full funding applications.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Publish the scorecard</h3><p>Set baselines, targets, reporting dates and evidence links for each commitment.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Member review</h3><p>Present priorities, costs and trade-offs; record amendments and unresolved choices.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Start quarterly reporting</h3><p>Release the first status report with delays and correction actions stated directly.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Six delivery gates</p><h2>The same discipline for every major commitment.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Required answer</th><th>Stop condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. Need</td><td>What member need changes, and how is it verified?</td><td>No defined outcome or beneficiary</td></tr><tr><td>2. Case</td><td>What options, full costs, risks and alternatives were tested?</td><td>No whole-life cost or credible option comparison</td></tr><tr><td>3. Authority</td><td>Who can approve it, what conflicts apply and what funding is lawful?</td><td>Authority, conflict review or funding source unresolved</td></tr><tr><td>4. Delivery</td><td>Who owns procurement, milestones, evidence and variance?</td><td>No owner, schedule or procurement route</td></tr><tr><td>5. Operation</td><td>Who staffs, operates, maintains and renews it?</td><td>Operating capacity or recurring funding missing</td></tr><tr><td>6. Report</td><td>What result, cost, benefit and correction will members see?</td><td>No measurable benefit or reporting route</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>The costing boundary</h2><p>Unknown is not zero. A blank cost stays blank until the required scope, quote, staffing model or funding package exists. The quarterly report shows every unresolved cost, who owns it and when the evidence is due.</p></section>
